.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers a callback function that is invoked each time the server emits
a \f[CR]post_command\f[R] event on \f[CR]CHAN_OBSERVE\f[R] (channel 3).
Post\-command events fire immediately after the bash interpreter
finishes executing a command, including its exit status and execution
duration.
.PP
Only one post\-command callback may be registered at a time.
Calling this function again replaces the previous callback and userdata.
Pass NULL as \f[CR]cb\f[R] to unregister the callback entirely.
.PP
The callback is invoked from within \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] when a
post\-command event message is received and decoded.
The \f[CR]event\f[R] pointer is valid only for the duration of the
callback invocation; the caller must copy any data it needs to retain.
.PP
