.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]event\f[R] struct and all its string fields are owned by the
library and are freed after the callback returns.
Copy strings with \f[CR]strdup()\f[R] if they are needed beyond the
callback scope.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]seq\f[R] field correlates pre and post events for the same
command.
A post\-command event with \f[CR]seq=N\f[R] always follows a
pre\-command event with the same \f[CR]seq=N\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
If a command is terminated by a signal, \f[CR]signal_number\f[R] is set
to the signal value and \f[CR]exit_status\f[R] is set to
\f[CR]128 + signal\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]duration_ms\f[R] measures wall\-clock time, not CPU time.
For background commands, this is the time until the command completes,
not until it is launched.
.IP \(bu 2
Callbacks execute synchronously within \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R].
Keep callbacks short and non\-blocking to avoid delaying event
processing.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: callbacks are always invoked from the thread that calls
\f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R].
The library is not thread\-safe.
